From: qforge
Subject: [PATCH] scan out a client's pre-rotated buffer unrotated

On a panel the planes can't rotate, every game frame is turned by a
copy in gamescope (0028), synchronously in the compositor thread. Mesa
can do that copy in the client instead: with vk_wsi_wayland_prerotate
set, its Wayland WSI blits each present into a rotated buffer on the
game's own queue and tags it with the matching wl_surface buffer
transform. Under gamescope that covers X11 Vulkan games too, since the
gamescope WSI layer presents them through Mesa's Wayland WSI. gamescope
ignored the transform, so such a buffer was rotated a second time.

Carry the buffer transform with each commit. A commit whose transform
is the rotation the display needs (wl_output_transform 90/180/270 is
g_uPreRotation 1/2/3: Mesa's prerotate=90 copies with ROTATE_270, as
our blit does for rotation 1) is marked bPreRotated: the DRM backend
already places such a layer as its unrotated self and scans it out with
no rotation and no copy. It is sized as its unrotated self, and never
pre-emptively upscaled.

The composite samples layers in logical orientation, so a frame that
has to composite, and a screenshot or PipeWire capture, gets the layer
copied back unrotated first (once per
commit, cached per slot) and restored afterwards for the caller.

(qforge: perf, MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-10.)
